WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.509
- You and I talked about anxiety.

00:00:01.509 --> 00:00:03.230
How have you managed
this during quarantine?

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:04.570
'Cause everybody's kind
of managed it differently.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.070
I've been writing a lot.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:06.941
- That's awesome.

00:00:06.941 --> 00:00:08.380
Yeah, it's interesting.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.030
For me, you know, I've
always dealt with anxiety,

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:14.190
so going into lockdown, even
hypochondriac, which is great

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:17.401
for a pandemic when you're
a hypochondriac, girl!

00:00:17.401 --> 00:00:20.810
And my old sort of techniques
of like meditation,

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:23.270
and the barn's always
amazing, but it just,

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.750
I was still having a lot of
anxiety, if I'm being honest.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:29.730
And I started listening
to music as sort of,

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.460
when I couldn't drop into
meditation, I'd put on a record,

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:33.530
started listening to music,

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.530
and just wanting to listen all the time.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:37.580
And I started thinking about
sort of the relationship

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.370
between anxiety, mental
health, and creativity,

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:43.551
and how healing is creative,
and creativity is healing.

00:00:43.551 --> 00:00:47.510
And then that led into
this new podcast endeavor

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:48.860
about the power of music-

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:50.170
- It's called harmonics, right?

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:51.497
- [Beth] Yeah, it's called harmonics, and-

00:00:51.497 --> 00:00:53.099
- [Kelly] And so what
exactly happens on it?

00:00:53.099 --> 00:00:56.640
- So basically I talked to Glennon Doyle

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:57.750
who wrote "Untamed."

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.030
- I love!

00:00:59.030 --> 00:00:59.930
- Girl!

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:00.803
- I'm a cheetah!

00:01:00.803 --> 00:01:01.987
- I'm a cheetah!

00:01:01.987 --> 00:01:02.820
- I'm a cheetah!

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.640
- So she's the first episode.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:05.473
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:05.473 --> 00:01:06.306
- And you can listen.

00:01:06.306 --> 00:01:07.201
And she's incredible.

00:01:07.201 --> 00:01:09.053
And Brandi Carlile, who-

00:01:09.053 --> 00:01:10.420
- I love!

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:11.540
- [Beth] That duet you guys did-

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:12.690
- I've never been more vain.

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:14.468
I've never listened to
myself more than that duet.

00:01:14.468 --> 00:01:16.470
- You two have the best
voices of all time,

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:17.821
and putting them together.

00:01:17.821 --> 00:01:20.580
By the way, I played that
video over and over again.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.413
I told Brandi, I was like-

00:01:21.413 --> 00:01:22.246
- I'm like a million of the views.

00:01:22.246 --> 00:01:23.560
- It's on repeat.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:26.590
But I wanted to ask people
in the music industry,

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:28.880
but also people like Glennon Doyle, women,

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.240
how they handle this time, mental health,

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.210
what's happening in the world,

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:34.360
the division, in order
to bring people together,

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.317
promote love, and hopefully
provide some sort of healing.

00:01:37.317 --> 00:01:40.440
And selfishly, I get
to ask people like you

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.530
all the questions I wanna
know about what do you do

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:43.520
for your mental health on a day

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:44.740
when you don't wanna get out of bed?

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:46.540
- This is an awesome podcast.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:47.580
- I would love to have you on.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.413
- I would love to come in.

00:01:48.413 --> 00:01:49.246
You know who should have too,

00:01:49.246 --> 00:01:52.783
another Glennon Doyle-type
of figure, is Brene Brown.

00:01:52.783 --> 00:01:53.820
I love her.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.210
- Her podcast is amazing.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:56.360
- [Kelly] Yes, her TED talks.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:57.980
- Her TED talks too, everything.

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:00.120
Yeah, I would love, I have a dream list.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.010
This is season one.

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:02.887
I have like my dream list, but I-

00:02:02.887 --> 00:02:03.720
- [Kelly] It's a really
smart and important thing.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.410
- You know music and the power of healing.

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:06.610
I mean, and writing.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:08.030
Have you been writing music or poetry?

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:09.773
- I literally don't know how
anybody goes through anything

00:02:09.773 --> 00:02:12.090
horrible or big their life
without having an outlet

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.320
like I have with writing.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.153
Like even if it doesn't get,

00:02:14.153 --> 00:02:15.950
I was talking to Gwen the
other day on "The Voice."

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:16.783
And I was like,

00:02:16.783 --> 00:02:18.400
we're both writing right
now for our next albums.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.260
And it's like, even if no one
hears it, it's so therapeutic.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.770
It's so good for you,
just that's your outlet.

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:25.100
- And it's almost like, you know,

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:27.190
whether you're religious
or not, or spiritual,

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:28.760
whatever you believe,
there's something about

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:30.940
that you're giving that
gift of your writing,

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:32.110
even if nobody ever sees it.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:33.340
- And it's a little like Marie Kondo, too.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.340
You're letting it go.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.270
Like, thank you for the
experience; I'm done.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:37.520
- Yeah, totally.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.900
And I'm terrified for this
podcast because I'm usually

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:42.070
like the girl twerking
upside down on television,

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:43.566
and like falling down the stairs.

00:02:43.566 --> 00:02:45.625
That's me, and everybody knows it.

00:02:45.625 --> 00:02:46.852
- There's room for all of it, Beth.

00:02:46.852 --> 00:02:49.690
- But I realize that,
like, if I expect my guests

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.950
to come on and not talk about, you know,

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:54.110
not just the classic sort
of interview questions,

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.630
if I want them to get vulnerable
and honest, then I had to.

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:59.470
And so I revealed some stuff,

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.540
and talked really deeply
about my mental health.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:04.970
But then hearing like that
other musicians that I admire

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:06.467
have panic attacks
before they go on stage.

00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:08.550
- Oh my gosh, especially musicians.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:09.744
- Yes, we'll talk through it.

00:03:09.744 --> 00:03:12.510
Brandi and I talked about when
she sang for Joni Mitchell,

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:14.403
and how, you know, turning blue.

00:03:14.403 --> 00:03:15.765
- I just started sweating
for her right now.

00:03:15.765 --> 00:03:16.903
Wow.

00:03:16.903 --> 00:03:19.790
- But if she can get through
that, I can get there.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:21.560
You know, there's something
about coming together

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:24.290
and speaking about mental health
openly, which for so long,

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.600
especially as women, we're
like, I can toughen up.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.540
You know, I'm gonna
take care of my family,

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:29.844
I'm going to take care
of everybody around me.

00:03:29.844 --> 00:03:30.777
- "Untamed," it's all in that book.

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:32.200
- [Beth] "Untamed"; cheetah.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.130
- I know.

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.530
- So yeah, it's been amazingly
healing selfishly for me,

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:37.987
but also I hope it helps other people.

